@startuml
title Feature flow - example: lesson list and mutation
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
actor User
participant "Screen / components" as UI
participant "Feature hook / query cache" as Hook
participant "Feature API + mapper" as API
participant "Authenticated HTTP client" as HTTP
participant Backend
User -> UI : Open lessons
UI -> Hook : Load lessons(accountId, filters)
Hook -> API : Fetch lessons
API -> HTTP : GET / feature endpoint
HTTP -> Backend : Request + bearer token
Backend --> HTTP : Response DTOs
HTTP --> API : Response DTOs
API -> API : DTOs -> Lesson[]
API --> Hook : Frontend models
Hook --> UI : Data / loading / error / empty
UI --> User : Render
User -> UI : Submit lesson form
UI -> Hook : Submit form model
Hook -> API : Validated input
API -> API : Form model -> request DTO
API -> HTTP : Mutation request
HTTP -> Backend : Request + bearer token
Backend --> HTTP : Success / structured error
HTTP --> API : Result
API --> Hook : Model / typed error
alt success
  Hook -> Hook : Update / invalidate affected queries
  Hook --> UI : Updated data
else validation / business error
  Hook --> UI : Field / operation errors; retain draft
end
note over UI,API
Components never depend on transport DTOs.
Styling changes do not change this flow.
end note
@enduml
